1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
Would you admit this student?

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,900
A 3.3 GPA.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,900
A 1280 SAT.

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,700
Not exactly the strongest
numbers in the room.

5
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:13,000
But they started a neighborhood
food-waste initiative,

6
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:15,220
built a local
food-donation guide,

7
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:18,250
and work 15 hours a week
at a grocery store.

8
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,400
Their grades dropped
sophomore year.

9
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,250
Then they started improving.

10
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:25,450
No major awards.
No prestigious internship.

11
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:27,150
So what matters more?

12
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,980
The numbers on the application…

13
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,850
…or what the student actually
did with their time?

14
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:33,400
You're the admissions committee.

15
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:35,050
Admit, or reject?

16
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:37,120
Defend your decision
in the comments.
